WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.750
George Catlin is working
on a different scale.

2
00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:06.160
He travels through the Great Plains
in the 1830s,

3
00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:11.790
painting hundreds of portraits and scenes
of Mandan, Hidatsa, Blackfeet, Crow,

4
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.290
and many other nations.

5
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.580
He describes his mission
as "rescuing from oblivion" the looks

6
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.940
and customs of peoples he believed
were vanishing,

7
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.630
even while he was documenting
vibrant living cultures.

8
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.670
And that's the contradiction.

9
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.460
He preserves invaluable images,
but frames his subjects through a narrative

10
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.010
of inevitable disappearance
that denies Native continuity and survival.
